claimed: okay-script-live -- operator ask 2026-09-06: okay-ui as the front-end layer for Site pages. A page declares a server-driven okay-ui app (Live(init)(view)(update), the okay.ui Wire.serve shape) in a ```scala declare block and mounts it in prose with ${mount("id", app)}: the mount renders view(init) to HTML server-side (React.elem -> HTML, so the page is complete without JS), plus a script tag; Site serves /__okay/live.js (a small dependency-free JS patch consumer speaking WireJson) and a WebSocket route site.ws (Jetty.serve(port)(site.routes)(site.ws)) at the page's own path + ?__live=<id> that runs Wire.serve over Frame.Text lines. Classloader: okay.* (except okay.script.* other than okay.script.api) joins the delegated prefixes so a page's Ui tree IS the host's. Touches build.sbt (okayScript gains okayUi.jvm main dep), ScalaScript/Site/Api, specs.
